# Raw asset packs kept locally but never committed - too large, and the game
# only needs the trimmed subsets checked in beside them.
# TopDown Vehicles is 26,776 PNGs; public/assets/packs/topdown-vehicles/ holds
# the 88 sheets actually used (see src/game/packs/topDownVehicles.js).
public/assets/packs/TopDown Vehicles v1.17/
public/assets/packs/Harvest Sumer Free Ver. Pack/
public/assets/packs/Pixel 16 v2 village free/

# Raw AI-generated NPC reference sheets: baked-in titles/grid-lines/labels and
# solid white backgrounds, unusable as game sprites as-is (see
# src/game/packs/npcRealSprites.js's header). Salvaged, game-ready sheets are
# cropped from these by hand and committed under packs/npc/processed/ instead
# - only that subfolder is tracked, not the raw originals sitting beside it.
public/assets/packs/npc/*.png

# Same deal for the police battle reference sheets: white-background contact
# sheets with several sprites plus a text caption under each. The individual
# sprites cut out of them live in packs/police-battle/ (no space in the path,
# so they're usable as plain URLs) and that folder IS committed.
public/assets/packs/police fighting/

# packs/Lisa/ raw sources. Everything the game actually loads is generated
# from these into two committed subfolders - packs/Lisa/processed/ (the
# overworld walk sprite sheet) and packs/Lisa/portraits/ + packs/Lisa/scenes/
# (the interaction UI). The raws stay local: they're large full-res stills,
# and several are real press photographs rather than the AI-generated art the
# game uses, so they should not be redistributed with the repo.
public/assets/packs/Lisa/*.png
public/assets/packs/Lisa/Lisa no bg/
public/assets/packs/Lisa/Lisa w bg/
public/assets/packs/Lisa/Background/

# Same deal for packs/Warren/ and packs/Ince/ (WarrenModal.jsx/IncModal.jsx) -
# raw full-res AI-generated stills with a solid white background. Only the
# processed cutouts under portraits/ are committed; both reuse packs/Lisa/
# scenes/ for backdrops rather than needing their own.
public/assets/packs/Warren/*.png
public/assets/packs/Ince/*.png

# packs/player/ raw sources - the four hand-supplied direction stills the
# player's sprite is built from (three are JPEGs despite the .png names).
# Only the salvaged sheet under processed/ is committed; rebuild it with
# `node production/salvagePlayerSprite.mjs`, which documents every transform.
public/assets/packs/player/raw/

# "lisa house"/"ince house" raw sources - full-res AI-generated building
# illustrations (white background, no game-ready alpha) used to remodel
# home_lisa and build the new inceHome facade. The salvaged, background-
# removed output actually loaded by the game lives under
# public/assets/buildings/ (home_lisa.png / home_ince.png, tracked normally
# alongside the other bespoke building facades there) - rebuild it with
# `python production/process_house_facades.py`, which documents every
# transform. The "lisa house" pack's second file (a garden-decor prop sheet)
# isn't currently used in-game - kept here for a possible future pass.
public/assets/packs/lisa house/
public/assets/packs/ince house/

# Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free - same deal again: raw full-res AI-generated
# furniture/prop stills (white background), used to furnish the 87 character
# home interiors (OverworldScene.js's HOME_ROOM_KITS/buildHomeInteriorZone).
# Only the pieces actually used are salvaged, under processed/ (tracked
# normally) - rebuild the single-subject ones with
# `python production/process_home_furniture.py`; the rest (floor swatches,
# wardrobe, palace banquet table, the whole hideout pedestal/bookshelf set,
# etc.) were picked by hand out of the _sliced_*/ directories (items.png,
# "walls and stair.png", 73.png, 85.png, and "tiles and items.png" -
# connected-component-sliced by `python production/slice_contact_sheet.py`) -
# regenerate those dirs with that script, then re-copy whichever pieces
# processed/ needs by index (see each HOME_FURNITURE_FILES entry's own name
# for which).
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/*.png
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/_sliced_items/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/_sliced_walls/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/_sliced_73/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/_sliced_85/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/_sliced_tiles/
# RPGMAKERMV/mv (RPG Maker character sheets, a different asset category
# bundled in the same download) and reference/ (the pack's own marketing
# screenshots) - neither is used by anything in src/.
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/RPGMAKERMV/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/mv/
public/assets/packs/Pixel_16_interiors_v2_free/reference/
